<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#khwarazmshah">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khwarazmshah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khwarazmshah ('Shah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazm">Khwarazm</a>') was the title of the rulers of Khwarazm, the oasis region on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aral-sea">Aral Sea</a>. It was borne by the Afrighid kings, then by the Ma'munids from 995, by Ghaznavid and Seljuq governors, and finally by the Anushtegin dynasty, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a> was destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1219–1221.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah.jpg" alt="Khwarazmshah" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circa 1425 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Takash,_Sultan_of_Khwarazm,_Congratulated_by_Rashid_al-Din-i_Vatvat,_Yale_University_Art_Gallery,_accession_number_1983-94-10_(Takash_portrait).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
